@scene chapter_6_riddle_weaver

background: night_valley.avif
music: mystery_forest.mp3

dialogue:
"The web thins, and the path turns up the bare rock toward the tower."
"Ahead a final gate stands sealed, a long ribbon of runes across its face."

background: riddle_weaver

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"THE RIDDLE WEAVER"
"Weave a name from the ribbon of runes."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"No loom here, child, and no second thread. Only the gate, and what you carry."
"Cut the first few runes of a long word, and you may hold a truer name hidden inside it."
"Then do not merely SHOW it, cold and bare. WEAVE it — your own words wrapped snug around the name you found."
"The gate hides a name in its first four runes. Slice it loose, then weave it into the words that open the way:"
"'The gate opens for —' and then the name, and a full stop, like a knot tied off."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Slice the first 4 runes as the name, then weave into opening_words: The gate opens for {name}."

mission: riddle_strings

background: forest_gate.png

dialogue:
"You cut the first four runes loose — a name, at last — wrap your words around them, and speak."
"The runes rearrange to match, and the gate swings open."

background: night_forest.avif

dialogue:
"Beyond it, far up a leaning tower on the bare rock, a single window burns gold."

npc Riddle Weaver:
"There. Cut, and woven, and spoken true. A weaver, then — not an apprentice."
"Go up. The lazy one is the last teacher on this road, and the strangest."
"He will try to give you everything and climb out of doing so. Let him. It is his only real magic."

dialogue:
"High above, the golden window burns on, patient, and the long climb begins in earnest."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Riddle Weaver"
"Applied: string slicing · f-strings"

reward:
xp: 100
gold: 50
achievement: WEAVER OF NAMES

next:
chapter_7b_spellbook
